{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2SchurWeylForeclosure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2SchurWeylForeclosure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.su2_index_ne_wlambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.su2_index_ne_wlambda","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/Su2SchurWeylForeclosure.lean#L90-L105","doc":"**Foreclosure of the SU(2)/WRT(S³/2I) route (the keystone result of this file).**\nAny weight system `idx` supported on the GL₂ Schur–Weyl image (vanishing off the ≤2-row\nblocks — the SU(2)-side WRT modular data) **differs** from any `W` that is nonzero on the\nelectron block `(3,1,1)`.\n\nApplied to the q-Plancherel weight `W = W_λ`, whose value on the electron block is\n`d_q(3,1,1)²/[5]_q! > 0` at the substrate (`hW`), this says the geometric `W_λ` index\n**cannot** be the naive SU(2)/WRT(S³/2I) modular data — it must live on the full-Hecke\nside. Abstract over the codomain `R`; positivity of `W_λ(3,1,1)` enters only via `hW`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.gl2_image_has_coverage_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.gl2_image_has_coverage_gap","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/Su2SchurWeylForeclosure.lean#L85-L88","doc":"The SU(2) side **omits at least one block** of `S₅` (the coverage gap). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.electron_not_in_gl2_image","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.electron_not_in_gl2_image","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/Su2SchurWeylForeclosure.lean#L79-L83","doc":"The **electron block `(3,1,1)`** (3 rows; carries the central A₅ rep `T₁ ⊕ T₂`) is\n**not** in the GL₂ Schur–Weyl image. The rigorous form of the ✅-forced corpus fact\n\"spinor ℂ² kills the electron (3,1,1)\" (#2406). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.gl2_image_eq_le2row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.gl2_image_eq_le2row","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/Su2SchurWeylForeclosure.lean#L73-L77","doc":"The GL₂ Schur–Weyl image among the partitions of 5 is **exactly** the three ≤2-row\nblocks `{(5),(4,1),(3,2)}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.instDecidableInGL2SchurWeylImage","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.instDecidableInGL2SchurWeylImage","kind":"instance","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/Su2SchurWeylForeclosure.lean#L70-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.PartitionOf5.inGL2SchurWeylImage","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.PartitionOf5.inGL2SchurWeylImage","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/Su2SchurWeylForeclosure.lean#L65-L68","doc":"A block lies in the **GL₂ (spinor ℂ²) Schur–Weyl image** iff its Young diagram has at\nmost two rows — `(ℂ²)^{⊗n} = ⊕_{λ:≤2 rows} S^λ ⊗ V_λ`.  This is the support of the\nSU(2)-side WRT(S³/2I) modular data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.PartitionOf5.numRows","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.PartitionOf5.numRows","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/Su2SchurWeylForeclosure.lean#L55-L63","doc":"Number of (nonzero) rows of the Young diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.PartitionOf5.allList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.PartitionOf5.allList","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/Su2SchurWeylForeclosure.lean#L51-L53","doc":"All 7 partitions of 5. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.instReprPartitionOf5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.instReprPartitionOf5","kind":"instance","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/Su2SchurWeylForeclosure.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.instReprPartitionOf5.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.instReprPartitionOf5.repr","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/Su2SchurWeylForeclosure.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.instDecidableEqPartitionOf5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.instDecidableEqPartitionOf5","kind":"instance","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/Su2SchurWeylForeclosure.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.PartitionOf5.onesFive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.PartitionOf5.onesFive","kind":"ctor","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/Su2SchurWeylForeclosure.lean#L48-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.PartitionOf5.twoOneOneOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.PartitionOf5.twoOneOneOne","kind":"ctor","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/Su2SchurWeylForeclosure.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.PartitionOf5.twoTwoOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.PartitionOf5.twoTwoOne","kind":"ctor","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/Su2SchurWeylForeclosure.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.PartitionOf5.threeOneOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.PartitionOf5.threeOneOne","kind":"ctor","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/Su2SchurWeylForeclosure.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.PartitionOf5.threeTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.PartitionOf5.threeTwo","kind":"ctor","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/Su2SchurWeylForeclosure.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.PartitionOf5.fourOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.PartitionOf5.fourOne","kind":"ctor","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/Su2SchurWeylForeclosure.lean#L43-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.PartitionOf5.five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.PartitionOf5.five","kind":"ctor","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/Su2SchurWeylForeclosure.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.PartitionOf5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Su2Foreclosure.PartitionOf5","kind":"inductive","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/Su2SchurWeylForeclosure.lean#L39-L49","doc":"The 7 partitions of 5 (indexing the 7 irreps of `S₅`); mirrors the keystone scaffold's\n`QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}